@startuml ProximaDB Collection State Machine
!theme plain
title ProximaDB - Collection Lifecycle State Machine Diagram

[*] --> Creating : create_collection()

state Creating
Creating : Validating config
Creating : Allocating resources
Creating : Creating metadata

state Initializing
Initializing : Setting up storage
Initializing : Creating indexes
Initializing : Configuring quantization

state Active {
  state Healthy
  Healthy : All systems go
  Healthy : Optimal performance
  
  state Degraded
  Degraded : Partial functionality
  Degraded : Some indexes offline
  Degraded : Performance impact
  
  state ReadOnly
  ReadOnly : No writes allowed
  ReadOnly : Queries still work
  ReadOnly : Maintenance mode
  
  Healthy --> Degraded : index failure
  Degraded --> Healthy : recovery complete
  Healthy --> ReadOnly : maintenance mode
  ReadOnly --> Healthy : maintenance complete
}

state Migrating
Migrating : Schema update
Migrating : Reindexing
Migrating : Storage migration

state Backing_Up
Backing_Up : Creating snapshot
Backing_Up : Copying data
Backing_Up : Preserving state

state Restoring
Restoring : Loading backup
Restoring : Rebuilding indexes
Restoring : Verifying integrity

state Deleting
Deleting : Removing data
Deleting : Cleaning indexes
Deleting : Releasing resources

state Deleted
Deleted : Metadata removed
Deleted : Storage released
Deleted : Tombstone period

Creating --> Initializing : config valid
Creating --> [*] : validation failed

Initializing --> Active : setup complete
Initializing --> [*] : setup failed

Active --> Migrating : schema change
Active --> Backing_Up : backup triggered
Active --> Deleting : delete request

Migrating --> Active : migration complete
Migrating --> Active : migration failed\n[rollback]

Backing_Up --> Active : backup complete
Backing_Up --> Active : backup failed

Restoring --> Active : restore complete
Restoring --> [*] : restore failed

Deleting --> Deleted : cleanup complete
Deleted --> [*] : retention expired

note right of Creating
  Validation checks:
  - Dimension valid
  - Name unique
  - Storage available
  - Index compatible
end note

note left of Migrating
  Migration scenarios:
  - Add filterable columns
  - Change quantization
  - Update indexes
  - Switch storage engine
end note

note bottom of Active
  Health monitoring:
  - Vector count
  - Query latency
  - Index efficiency
  - Storage usage
end note

@enduml